# rule.always.scope-onetime-lessons-to-the-behavior

a lesson born inside a behavior has **two homes**, and most real incidents need both.

| tier | home | holds |
|---|---|---|
| **one-time** | `$behavior/` | the concrete, instance-bound result, with its evidence |
| **durable** | `.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/`, or another repo via radio | the repo-agnostic kernel |

**and the two link to each other.** the durable brief cites the behavior doc as its worked example; the behavior doc points up to the durable brief.

## .the discipline

1. **scope the instance** — the exact files, diffs, commands, failures — into `$behavior/`. it lives and dies with the behavior
2. **always attempt to generalize** — *"what is the durable, repo-agnostic kernel here?"* if there is one, distill it. the durable home may be **this** repo's briefs, or **another** repo's, via a radio task
3. **link back — both directions.** the durable brief: *"first seen in `<repo>/$behavior/<slug>`"*. the behavior doc: a pointer up

🟡 **a lesson whose home is another repo is re-seeded there, never adopted here.** a tree adopts only what is scoped to itself.

## .the test

| useful to… | then… |
|---|---|
| only someone who ran **this exact behavior** | behavior dir, full stop |
| a traveler in **any** repo | generalize into a durable brief, **and** link it back |
| **both** — the common case | capture both, linked |

⇒ **most real incidents are both.** the default is not a choice between homes; it is a pair of writes.

## .the anti-patterns

blocker: an instance-bound lesson in the durable dir · a durable kernel discarded with its behavior dir · a lesson whose durable home is another repo, adopted here. nitpick: a durable brief with no worked-example citation · a behavior doc with no pointer up.

⇒ `rule.always.externalize.lessons.into_briefs` is the WHETHER; this is the WHERE. `rule.require.timeless-lessons` binds the durable half too.
